Theorem L-4: Partial order reflexive antisymmetric transitive

  Preconditions:
    - a, b, c are AimsState elements per the canonical proof notation
    - Partial order le is defined as a le b iff join(a, b) = b per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-4

  Soundness property:
    Forall a, b, c in AimsState.
      reflexive: a le a
      antisymmetric: (a le b) and (b le a) implies a = b
      transitive: (a le b) and (b le c) implies a le c

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-02 lattice algebra proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice
      monotonicity

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-02 discharges L-4 partial order axioms

