Theorem TF-13: capture_state_update transfers closure-context state to captured variables

  Preconditions:
    - PartialApply captures vars per Annex E §AIMS TF-13
    - closure_state.locality drives access promotion (Borrowed plus
      HeapEscaping would let the closure outlive its source without Owned
      promotion)
    - closure cardinality le Once preserves linear; > Once widens to Unrestricted

  Soundness property:
    Forall captured var v, closure_state cs.
      cs.locality ge HeapEscaping
        implies capture_state_update(v.state, cs).access := Owned
      cs.cardinality le Once
        implies capture_state_update(v.state, cs) updates via
          consumption := seq_add(v.consumption, Affine);
          cardinality := seq_add(v.cardinality, Once);
          locality := max(v.locality, cs.locality)
      cs.cardinality > Once
        implies capture_state_update(v.state, cs) widens to Unrestricted, Many, max(loc).
    Result SHALL be monotone per L-6.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-04 transfer function proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis
      monotonicity
      lattice

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-04 discharges TF-13 capture_state_update

